Apps that travel with the system.

A folder here is an app's own release, unchanged: its files and its own
installer. rk-apps installs from it when the app's repository does not
publish a newer one, so the app is on a fresh card, reaches a card that is
updated and not flashed again (an update replaces /usr/share/rk), and
installs with no network.

  stump-rf-recon   STUMP Recon, the RK3326 Linux port (its VERSION file says which)

To bring in a new version: replace the folder with the app's release and
keep VERSION as its first line reads. Once the app's repository carries the
same layout on its main branch (VERSION, deploy/install.sh), rk-apps takes
whichever version is higher.
